# Homebrew Installation Guidance

- If required system packages/tools are missing, install them using Homebrew.
- Always invoke Homebrew commands as: `arch -arm64 brew <args>`
- Prefer `arch -arm64 brew update` before installing when installing toolchains/dev deps.
- Use `arch -arm64 brew install <pkg>` for formulae.
- Use `arch -arm64 brew install --cask <app>` for GUI apps (if needed).
- If something may already be installed, avoid reinstalling; verify first with `command -v <bin>` and/or `arch -arm64 brew list --formula` / `arch -arm64 brew list --cask`.

# Examples

```shell
arch -arm64 brew update
arch -arm64 brew install cmake
arch -arm64 brew install --cask iterm2
```
